# configure tool

Writes `out/config.mdy` without running another command. `--compiler` accepts
gcc, g++, clang, or clang++, optionally followed by a numeric major version.
`--build` accepts debug or release and defaults to debug. Build and test consume
the same persisted compiler and build selection. `--target-host` marks an
explicit target as capable of receiving both host-buildable and target-buildable
artifacts without changing any source manifest.
`--runner` accepts none or a compatible named profile. The qemu-user profile
configures qemu-m68k for m68k-linux-gnu target execution.
`--debugger` accepts none or gdb. It configures direct host GDB or, for the
supported m68k target, gdb-multiarch connected through the QEMU runner stub.
